function very
well, which is checking the timestamps to have large future (or past) =
dates.
How about a more descriptive name =93check_old_ext4_negative_epoch()=94 =
or
maybe =93check_inode_extra_negative_epoch()=94 or something like that?

> +	return (xtime & (1 << 31)) !=3D 0 &&
> +		(extra & EXT4_EPOCH_MASK) =3D=3D EXT4_EPOCH_MASK;
> +}
> +
> +#define LARGE_INODE_EXTRA(inode, xtime) \

Ditto.

> +	large_inode_extra(inode->i_##xtime, \
> +			  inode->i_##xtime##_extra)
> +
> +/* When the date is earlier than 2311, we assume that atimes, ctimes,
> + * and mtimes greater than 2311 are actually pre-1970 dates =
mis-encoded.

I like the idea of checking the current date, so that there isn=92t a =
need to
revert this code at some point in the future.  I=92m wondering if there =
should
be a margin, like =93When the current date is earlier than 2240 we =
assume ...
